---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const normalizeBidsResult = await normalizeBids(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const mapRequirementsResult = await mapRequirements(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, normalizeBidsResult.accepted);
const identifySeamsResult = await identifySeams(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, mapRequirementsResult.accepted);
const runClarificationsResult = await runClarifications(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, identifySeamsResult.accepted);
const freezeMatrixResult = await freezeMatrix(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, runClarificationsResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { normalizeBids: normalizeBidsResult, mapRequirements: mapRequirementsResult, identifySeams: identifySeamsResult, runClarifications: runClarificationsResult, freezeMatrix: freezeMatrixResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...normalizeBidsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...mapRequirementsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...identifySeamsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...runClarificationsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...freezeMatrixResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...normalizeBidsResult.checks, ...mapRequirementsResult.checks, ...identifySeamsResult.checks, ...runClarificationsResult.checks, ...freezeMatrixResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A bidder’s price includes an allowance rather than a firm quantity: preserve uncertainty in comparison. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve uncertainty in comparison.) through the existing stage result for BidScope; preserve exact source/version and the prior BidScope, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A clarification changes an exclusion: update all affected interface cells. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (update all affected interface cells.) through the existing stage result for BidScope; preserve exact source/version and the prior BidScope, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — Two trades each assume the other supplies a connection: create a named acceptance task. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (create a named acceptance task.) through the existing stage result for BidScope; preserve exact source/version and the prior BidScope, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A late bid revision removes an inclusion: invalidate the previous coverage finding. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (invalidate the previous coverage finding.) through the existing stage result for BidScope; preserve exact source/version and the prior BidScope, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A lower total omits commissioning: show functional incompleteness rather than ranking by price alone. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (show functional incompleteness rather than ranking by price alone.) through the existing stage result for BidScope; preserve exact source/version and the prior BidScope, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, normalizeBids: normalizeBidsResult, mapRequirements: mapRequirementsResult, identifySeams: identifySeamsResult, runClarifications: runClarificationsResult, freezeMatrix: freezeMatrixResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
